            <ArticleTitle>Diagnosis of Cystic Teratoma Facilitated by Point-of-Care Ultrasonography.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>558-60</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <ELocationID EIdType="doi" ValidYN="Y">10.1097/PEC.0000000000000875</ELocationID>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Abdominal pain and constipation are common chief complaints in the pediatric emergency department. We present a case of a child with pain, abdominal distention, and constipation ultimately diagnosed with an ovarian teratoma and the role of point-of-care ultrasonography in the evaluation.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
